# Gitleaks findings accepted in the public tree. One shell glob per line, matched
# against the tree-relative path (`*` also matches `/`). Every entry is test key
# material, a recorded oracle/golden vector, a vendored upstream reference, doc
# example text, or a reviewed literal (the 2026-11-13 scan, gitleaks 8.30.1, found no
# real secret). Read a new finding before adding its path; keep entries narrow.

# Rust conformance goldens, oracle recordings, test fixtures
server-rust/tests/conformance/*
server-rust/crates/protocols/smtp/oracle/*
server-rust/crates/protocols/federation/oracle/*
server-rust/bins/*/tests/*
server-rust/crates/*/tests/*
server-rust/crates/config-secret/src/tests.rs
# PEM header string matches in parsing code (no key material)
server-rust/bins/gateway/src/jmap/recovery.rs
server-rust/bins/gateway/src/recovery_begin.rs
# Go and SQL tests
*_test.go
mailserver/sql/tests/*.pg
mailserver/webmail/e2e/*.spec.ts
# Test and rehearsal scripts with fixed throwaway credentials
scripts/*.test.sh
scripts/*.test.mjs
scripts/test-scim.sh
scripts/test-secfix3-mutants.py
scripts/e6-gateway-fixture.sh
scripts/ga-fresh-install-smoke.sh
scripts/unified-deployment-d2.sh
mailserver/deploy/scripts/test-livekit-render.sh
# Model sha256 pins, not secrets
mailserver/deploy/scripts/lib-livekit.sh
# Code literals flagged by generic-api-key (key type, field names)
mailserver/internal/acme/dns01.go
mailserver/internal/user/migration.go
# Vendored upstream references and RFC text
clients/harmonyos/refs/openharmony-docs/*
clients/rust/refs/ios-security-framework/*
docs/ref/rfc/*
docs/ref/rfcs/*
# Documentation examples
docs/design/security/archive/env-security.md
docs/guides/INTEGRATION_EXAMPLES.md
docs/guides/acme-dns01.md
mailserver/internal/DOX.md
